  "scope_notes": [
    "After the complete matrix, affected workflows additionally verified unindexed worker fallback and missing map-message ProtoJSON defaults; both-target checks, builds and tests were then rerun.",
    "ProtoJSON is opt-in serialization mapping; no reverse JSON-to-wire encoder, GROUP, Editions or extension decoding.",
    "CDR is the documented plain XCDR1/ros2msg subset; XCDR2, IDL and wstring are not claimed.",
    "Async MIDX2 opens still audit all pages and hash the source by default. Warm HTTP cache reuse does not remove logical validation work.",
    "MFLD1 summaries must come from a trusted producer; CRC and a source digest are not signatures proving summary completeness.",
    "CJOB2 reuses committed final sorting/merge work, but final MCAP publication is restarted as a whole after interruption.",
    "Node workers are opt-in, consume additional RSS, and do not universally accelerate end-to-end queries. Payload/transport budgets are not RSS bounds.",
    "The complete 4719-message CDR comparison uses an independent serializer. The additional parallel-versus-serial comparison covers 200 messages and 4 topics.",
    "Public source data remains under its own terms and is not redistributed; reports distinguish synthetic data, native MCAP and raw-preserving ROS1 conversion."
  ]
